# Instant Mechanic — Live Operations Dashboard: Complete System Blueprint & Code Manual

This document provides a line-by-line and block-by-block technical reference for every file in the project. It explains **what each file does**, **why it is required by the system**, **how data flows through it**, and **how to modify it in the future**.

---

## 1. System Architecture & High-Level Data Flow

```
  +-----------------------------------------------------------------------+
  |                     REACT (VITE) FRONTEND CLIENT                      |
  |  (TanStack Query + Socket.io Client + Tailwind CSS + Lucide Icons)   |
  +-----------------------------------+-----------------------------------+
                                      |
                       HTTP REST API  |  Socket.io Events
                       (JSON Requests)|  (Real-Time Broadcasts)
                                      v
  +-----------------------------------------------------------------------+
  |                     NODE.JS + EXPRESS BACKEND SERVER                  |
  |      (connectDB + SocketManager + Controllers + Mongoose Models)      |
  +-----------------------------------+-----------------------------------+
                                      |
                                Mongoose ORM
                                      v
  +-----------------------------------------------------------------------+
  |                         MONGODB DATABASE                              |
  |  Collections: Customers | Mechanics | Services | Bookings (Text Indexed)|
  +-----------------------------------------------------------------------+
```

### Data Flow Scenario: Operational Booking Status Update
1. **User Action:** Ops dispatcher updates a booking from `Assigned` to `Mechanic On The Way` on the React UI board.
2. **HTTP Mutation:** Client sends `PATCH /api/bookings/:id/status` via Axios (`client/src/lib/api.ts`).
3. **Express Controller Execution:** `bookingController.updateBookingStatus` receives the request:
   - Updates `Booking` document status and appends a timestamped log to `statusHistory[]`.
   - Automatically updates assigned `Mechanic` status to `on_the_way`.
   - Saves both documents to MongoDB.
4. **Real-Time Broadcast:** Controller calls `notifyBookingUpdated(booking)` and `notifyMechanicStatusChanged(mechanic)` via `server/src/sockets/socketManager.ts`.
5. **Client Cache Invalidation:** `client/src/hooks/useSocketEvents.ts` hears `booking:updated` and calls `queryClient.invalidateQueries({ queryKey: ['bookings'] })`.
6. **Zero-Latency UI Sync:** All open dashboard browser windows automatically re-render the updated booking and mechanic state in real time without refreshing the page!

