## 2. Server Architecture (`server/`)

### 2.1 Database Connection (`server/src/config/connectDB.js`)

```javascript
import mongoose from 'mongoose';
import dotenv from 'dotenv';

dotenv.config();

export const connectDB = async () => {
  try {
    const mongoUri = process.env.MONGO_URI || process.env.MONGODB_URI;

    if (!mongoUri) {
      console.error('❌ [Database] Critical Error: MONGO_URI environment variable is missing in .env!');
      process.exit(1);
    }

    console.log('📡 [Database] Attempting connection to MongoDB...');
    const conn = await mongoose.connect(mongoUri);

    console.log(`✅ [Database] MongoDB Connected Successfully! Host: ${conn.connection.host}`);
    console.log(`📊 [Database] Database Name: ${conn.connection.name}`);
  } catch (error) {
    console.error(`❌ [Database] Connection Failure Error: ${error.message}`);
    process.exit(1);
  }
};

export default connectDB;
```
- **What it does:** Reads `MONGO_URI` from `.env`, initializes Mongoose connection, and logs host/database details.
- **Why required by system:** Prevents the Express server from accepting HTTP requests or socket clients when database connectivity fails. If the connection fails, it halts the process (`process.exit(1)`).

