### 37. Nginx Reverse Proxy & WebSocket Upgrading (`/etc/nginx/sites-available/instant-mechanic`)

```nginx
server {
    listen 80;
    server_name your-domain.com;

    location /api/ {
        proxy_pass http://127.0.0.1:5000/api/;
        proxy_http_version 1.1;
        proxy_set_header Host $host;
        proxy_set_header X-Real-IP $remote_addr;
        proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-For $proxy_add_x_forwarded_for;
        proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-Proto $scheme;
    }

    location /socket.io/ {
        proxy_pass http://127.0.0.1:5000/socket.io/;
        proxy_http_version 1.1;
        proxy_set_header Upgrade $http_upgrade;
        proxy_set_header Connection "upgrade";
        proxy_set_header Host $host;
        proxy_read_timeout 86400s;
        proxy_send_timeout 86400s;
    }
}
```
- **Why required:** Nginx handles SSL termination, gzip compression, request buffering, and WebSocket upgrade handshakes much more efficiently than a bare Node.js server.

